# Admin Dashboard — Complete Implementation Plan

## Goal
Build a full Admin Dashboard system for Mellow Cafe with:
1. **Full menu migration** from static `menu.js` to MongoDB
2. **Role-based access** (`user`, `worker`, `staff`, `admin`, `super_admin`)
3. **Admin Request flow** — anyone can request access; only `super_admin` (`hariiiiii0519@gmail.com`) can approve and assign roles
4. **Admin Portal login** on the Login page
5. **Admin Dashboard** with analytics, stock/menu management, and request management

---

## Overview of What Changes

| Layer | What changes |
|---|---|
| **Database** | New `Category`, `MenuItem`, `AdminRequest` models; `User` gets `role` field |
| **Backend** | New `/api/menu` and `/api/admin/*` routes; auth routes return `role` |
| **Frontend** | `menu.js` retired; menu fetched from API; Login page gets Admin flows; new Admin pages |

---

## Phase 1: Database — New & Updated Models

### [MODIFY] `Server/models/User.cjs`
Add `role` field to the existing schema:
```js
role: {
  type: String,
  enum: ['user', 'worker', 'staff', 'admin', 'super_admin'],
  default: 'user'
}
```
> Super Admin (`hariiiiii0519@gmail.com`) will have their role auto-set to `super_admin` at login time, not stored differently.

---

### [NEW] `Server/models/Category.cjs`
Mirrors the `categories` array in `menu.js`. Each document is one category:
```js
{
  id: String,          // e.g. "hot-cold" — used as slug
  name: String,        // "Hot & Cold Beverages"
  description: String,
  image: String,
  order: Number        // for controlling display order
}
```

---

### [NEW] `Server/models/MenuItem.cjs`
Mirrors each item in the `items` object in `menu.js`:
```js
{
  itemId: Number,      // original numeric ID from menu.js (1–98)
  categoryId: String,  // e.g. "hot-cold"
  name: String,
  price: Number,
  stock: Number,
  size: String,        // optional, e.g. "1/2 Kg"
  options: [String],   // optional flavor options, e.g. ["Vanilla", "Strawberry"]
}
```

---

### [NEW] `Server/models/AdminRequest.cjs`
Tracks admin access requests submitted from the Login page:
```js
{
  name: String,
  email: String,
  reason: String,       // optional — why they need access
  status: {
    type: String,
    enum: ['pending', 'approved', 'rejected'],
    default: 'pending'
  },
  assignedRole: String,  // set by super_admin when approving
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

